<p>Two ways to show a thing before it is there. The <strong>skeleton</strong> is the page’s own loading shapes (<a href="/components/loading/">im-skeleton</a>) sized in the frame’s em: bones for a title, a line, a chip, a picture, shimmering. Put the skeleton and the content in one <code>im-studio-resolve</code> cell and the skeleton dissolves at <code>--im-studio-resolve-at</code> (2s). The <strong>blueprint</strong> draws every child of a stage as a dashed outline in the accent first, grey and flat, and lets the fill arrive — a wireframe becoming the real thing.</p>
